==============================================================================
GATE -- is the thesis's two-potential formulation correct?
  reference + contrast (solved)  vs  contrast folded into the background
  the second is exact for this medium; agreement is the correctness test
  contrast Dlam=2.0 Dmu=1.0 GPa, Drho=0.1 g/cm3, laterally uniform
  ka = 0.094  (the cube T-matrix is validated for ka < 0.3)
==============================================================================

    n_x   sites   thesis ordering    dress-after
      6      36        2.0649e-02     1.5047e-02
     10     100        2.8401e-02     1.8024e-02
     14     196        2.7202e-02     2.0789e-02

  DISCRETISATION CONTROL -- uniform background, formulation removed
      n_x     residual
        6   2.1021e-02
       10   2.5903e-02
       14   1.6458e-02

  discretisation residual is small enough to conclude: NO
    The discretisation error is comparable to the quantity being
    measured, so NOTHING above is evidence about the formulation.
    Two known causes, both documented in this repository: a finite
    patch is not a layer (the slab convergence study reached ~1%
    only with a periodic Weyl sum, an INFINITE layer), and
    space-filling cubes touch, where the point propagator is known
    to differ from the volume-averaged one.

==============================================================================
  thesis ordering improves with lattice size : NO
  dress-after separated by >10x at the widest: NO

  The lateral truncation is a real error, not noise: a finite patch of
  scatterers is not a layer. Refinement is the only honest reading, and
  a single lattice size would prove nothing.

  A thesis-ordering error that does NOT fall under refinement is a
  REFUTATION, and would point at the stratified propagator or the
  composition rather than at the ordering.

  VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE (discretisation-limited). Superseded by
  scripts/gate_thesis_formulation_periodic.py, which settles the question.
==============================================================================
